{
  "name": "swim_down",
  "//": "SWIMMING DOWN (Ctrl under water): a head-first dive. The hips pitch the body 115 degrees, past horizontal, so the head leads the descent; the same breaststroke as swim_up pulls toward the feet, and the legs dolphin-kick together. Blended with `swim` by the vertical share of the travel, so a shallow forward descent pitches part way between the two. Rotations: hips = lean Z (+ = right) of pitch X (+ = forward) of roll Y; every other part = sweep Y of flex X of abduction Z. A hanging limb: X negative = forward/up, positive = back; Z negative = the RIGHT limb out from the side. Knees +X bend, elbows -X bend. Hips pos in decimetres. All six swim clips share one 1200 ms period and one playhead (pose.cpp, the swim family), so a blend of two directions strokes in step.",
